          "heading": "Stuart McCloskey says he couldn't care less about Ireland's ageing midfield",
          "body": "Ulster centre Stuart McCloskey, one of four 30-somethings in a long-running midfield contest, was asked this week about the ageing of Ireland's centres and was unconcerned. \"Honestly, I couldn't care less about the succession of what's going on after me,\" he told reporters in Abbotstown. The worry is a fair one: the XV that beat Argentina 42-12 last weekend averaged 29.2 years, with eight players aged 30 or over."
