          "heading": "Townsend stresses 'individual responsibility' after seven tries conceded to New Zealand",
          "body": "Gregor Townsend says Scotland's problems against New Zealand were more about how they let the All Blacks into their 22 than about defence itself. He accepted that players coming offside or not rolling away quickly are part of the defence, but framed them as individual responsibility. Scotland conceded seven tries in the 21-43 defeat, and Townsend noted that the best teams in the world look to score over 50% of the time from those entries."
