          "heading": "Warner Dearns to co-captain Japan after Hurricanes' Super Rugby title",
          "body": "Japan second row Warner Dearns starts Saturday as co-captain. The 6ft 8in lock moved from Hawke's Bay in New Zealand at 14 when his father took a strength and conditioning job at NEC Green Rockets, and recalls: \"I said I didn't want to go.\" He made his Japan debut in November 2021, aged 19, and after a sabbatical season with the Hurricanes he helped Wellington win their first Super Rugby title in a decade."
