          "heading": "Frank Bunce says Jordie Barrett, Quinn Tupaea not far from Springboks centres",
          "body": "Former All Blacks centre Frank Bunce says Jordie Barrett is \"in the conversation for being one of the best in the world\". Quinn Tupaea, who impressed at 13 late in 2025, has very much nailed down the jersey under New Zealand head coach Dave Rennie. Bunce told Sport Nation the Springboks pair of Damian de Allende and Jesse Kriel are \"possibly not quite as good yet\", but insists they are not far off. New Zealand have struggled for a settled midfield since Ma'a Nonu and Conrad Smith retired."
